  "contracts": {
    "zoomIn": "0x50a6e0 doubles zoom up to16; visible center from min+X*step, else midpoint; new range +/-oldwidth/4; center strict1..499 after projection; active measurement reprojects both stored Extended shoulders",
    "zoomOut": "0x50a8c4 halves zoom; marker/cached center; range +/-oldwidth,full bounds at1; active measurement reprojects stored shoulder wavelengths",
    "pan": "0x50aab4/0x50ac88 shift10percent and bound range; reproject center; active-measurement pair projects only if right wavelength<=maximum and left wavelength>=minimum,otherwise both shoulder X clear. These writes do not clear Extended wavelength/continuum scalars",
    "reset": "0x50ae60 restores full bounds and zoom1; reprojects center when present and both shoulder wavelength fields when active",
    "paint": "0x5081e4..0x5081ee calls center then shoulder painting; center paint calls right-then-left guard. Shoulder paint requires positive X. Pixel/sentinel behavior is not independently portable as simple SVG clipping"
  },
  "implemented": [
    "Existing classificationViewport interval policy reused, default3900..4500 only;Number,nearest-even range endpoints and marker-column zoom anchor remain its existing declared adapter",
    "Manual graph gets independent ephemeral viewport; visible window drives existing printed-point crop and continuous SVG/manual coordinate conversion; no sample interpolation or normalized-source-value inference added",
    "Explicit marked center is zoom anchor; off-window cursor marks hidden individually, retained scientific draft strings survive all view actions and redraw on return",
    "Pointer snapshot includes viewport identity; all view actions clear/release held and keyboard preview. Source changes remount/reset. Numeric fields,records,integrator,JSON/CSV and source authority unchanged",
    "Existing keyboard1/10Angstrom and.01/.1intensity steps clamp to visible manual window; mobile3axislabels are authored presentation"
  ],
  "remainingNativeContracts": [
    "Native500column/sentinel/Extendedscalar vs X/Y separation and asymmetriczoom-in/out/reset event ordering; no integer pixel equivalence",
    "Native paired pan clearing plus center-paint revalidation after projection; this browser increment clips individual off-window marks and does not claim that native lifecycle",
    "Shared comparison/photo-pane Y geometry,pane inversion/focus/global configuration and native GDI,VCL modal/format behavior",
    "ScientificNumber/x87differences and known independent integration residual limits remain;no persistent schema,grade or wider measurement-domain change"
  ],
  "uncertainty": "Read-only static evidence. No original execution,emulation or resource addition; existing CLEA/Gettysburg credits/license uncertainty retained. Browser clipping/state safety are explicit adapters,not recovered native visual equivalence."
